[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m cd c_src
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m grep -nE 'return|assert|NULL|errno|exit\(|abort|if|switch|while|for|else|goto|#if|%:if|ERROR|error|<|>|MIN|MAX|limits' -r src include
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The only hits are the include guard (`%:ifndef DRIVER_H_` / `%:endif`), the two
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `%:include` lines, and the two brace digraphs of `driver`'s own body. Full list
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m of hits:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m src/driver.c:26:%:include <stdio.h>
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m src/driver.c:27:%:include <iso646.h>
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m src/driver.c:29:void driver(int x, int y) <%
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m src/driver.c:33:%>
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m include/driver.h:24:%:ifndef DRIVER_H_
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m include/driver.h:29:%:endif //DRIVER_H_
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
