[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m one exported symbol, `driver`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axes the C actually branches on:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **runtime options / modes / flags**: none. There is no init function, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   context/handle struct, no setter, no global, no environment variable read, and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   no `if`/`switch` anywhere in `src/driver.c`. The grep in `ERRORS.md` shows the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   only preprocessor conditional in the subtree is the `DRIVER_H_` include guard,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   so there is no `#ifdef`-selected behaviour either.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **compile-time features**: none (`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **input shapes**: the two `int` parameters. `int` is 32-bit two's complement on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the target, so the shape axes the code's behaviour actually depends on are the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   *bit patterns* of `x` and `y` (feeding `x | ~y`) and, via `printf("%d", …)`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the *sign* and *decimal digit width* of the result.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **call-sequence shape**: `driver` is stateless, but it writes to the shared
