[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the number and ordering of successive calls is a genuine observable axis
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`empty / one / many`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The rows below are the pruned cross-product of those axes: the boundary values of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m each parameter against each other, the classes that make the result's sign and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m digit width vary, the algebraically special pairs (`y = 0` ⇒ `~y = -1` ⇒ result
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `-1` for any `x`; `x = -1` ⇒ result `-1` for any `y`; `x = 0, y = -1` ⇒ result
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `0`), full-range random bit patterns, and the call-count axis.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row is driven through **both** `.so` files loaded with `libloading` and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m real `stdout` bytes are captured and compared. Rows marked *(randomized)* run
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m many pseudorandom inputs from a fixed-seed SplitMix64 generator, so they are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reproducible.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |----|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1  | `driver` | no options (none exist); `x = 0`, `y = 0` — zero/zero boundary, result `-1` | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2  | `driver` | `x = 0`, `y = -1` — the unique pair whose result is `0` (1-digit non-negative output) | [x] |
